# Build-context excludes for `DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker build -f infra/Dockerfile .` ONLY.
#
# **BUILDKIT IS A PREREQUISITE, not a detail.** Only BuildKit reads a
# <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore sitting next to the Dockerfile; the legacy
# builder ignores per-Dockerfile ignore files entirely and looks only for a
# context-root .dockerignore -- and there is deliberately none in this repo
# (see the next paragraph). So a non-BuildKit build of this image applies NO
# exclusions at all: the whole repo, .git and node_modules and any local .env
# included, goes into the build context, and everything below stops being
# true. Docker 23+ enables BuildKit by default, but infra/runbooks/
# deploy-ec2.md's build command still sets DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 explicitly
# rather than relying on the daemon's default.
#
# BuildKit reads that per-Dockerfile file in preference to a context-root
# .dockerignore. That scoping is the entire reason this file is here rather
# than at the repo root: this
# image builds from the ROOT context (it needs backend/, ontology/ and
# frontend/ at once), and a root .dockerignore would also have changed what
# the LEGACY root ./Dockerfile -- the Streamlit app, untouched by this phase
# -- sees in its own `COPY . .`.
#
# Two jobs: keep host-only trees out of the context (frontend/node_modules
# alone is ~157 MB, and none of it is used -- stage 1 runs its own `npm ci`),
# and make it structurally impossible for a real secret to reach the image.

# Host-only / regenerated trees.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
# The SPA is BUILT inside stage 1; a stale host dist must never leak in and
# masquerade as the bundle this image was built from.
frontend/dist

# Secrets. .env is gitignored, so it exists only on a developer's machine --
# exactly the file that must never be baked into a shipped image. The
# container's configuration comes from the orchestrator's environment, and
# infra/docker-compose.ec2.yml sets POSEIDON_ENV_FILE="" so Settings reads no
# dotenv at all. .env.example is re-admitted: it is documentation, carries
# only placeholders, and is tracked in git.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Documentation, planning and tooling trees -- context weight with no
# runtime use.
docs
.superpowers
.claude
.maestro
.streamlit
.playwright-mcp
.github
*.png
